  "notes": [
    "Irregular -ER verb with an *o→ue* stem change (same pattern as *poder*, *volver*, *dormir*): the stressed *o* in the stem becomes *ue* everywhere except nosotros/nosotras and the preterite/imperfect/future/conditional, which stay regular",
    "Nosotros forms always revert to the unstressed stem: *mordemos* (Presente), *mordamos* (Subjuntivo/Imperativo)",
    "Past participle: *mordido* (regular)",
    "Means \"to bite\" — *el perro me mordió* (the dog bit me), *muerde la manzana* (bite the apple)",
    "Reflexive *morderse* is common for body parts: *se mordió la lengua* (he/she bit his/her tongue — also figuratively \"held his/her tongue\")",
    "Related: *mordida* (bite, also \"bribe\" in some Latin American countries), *mordedura* (bite wound), *mordaz* (biting, sarcastic)"
  ],
